  "result": "Perfect! \u2705 The refactoring is complete and successful. Here's what was done:\n\n## Refactoring Summary\n\n### 1. **Created `src/totals.js`**\nExtracted four functions and their dependencies:\n- `lineTotal(line)` \u2014 Calculate qty \u00d7 unitPrice\n- `lineDiscount(line)` \u2014 Calculate discount amount\n- `lineVAT(line)` \u2014 Calculate VAT on discounted amount\n- `invoiceTotals(invoice)` \u2014 Calculate all invoice totals\n\nThese functions use only `roundCents()` from money.js as a dependency.\n\n### 2. **Updated `src/invoices.js`**\n- Removed the function definitions\n- Added import from `src/totals.js`\n- Re-exported all four functions to maintain backward compatibility\n- Removed unused `roundCents` import\n\n### 3. **Created `test/totals.test.js`**\nAdded 35 comprehensive tests covering:\n- **lineTotal:** basic calculation, rounding, fractional cents, edge cases\n- **lineDiscount:** no discount case, percentage calculations, decimal percentages, 0% and 100%, clamping at 0\n- **lineVAT:** VAT calculation with/without discount, various rates (21%, 9%, 0%), rounding, clamping\n- **invoiceTotals:** single/multiple lines, discounts, VAT, vouchers, mixed rates, empty arrays, structure validation\n\n### Results\n- **352 tests passing** (317 original + 35 new)\n- **Backward compatible:** Everything importable from `src/invoices.js` before still works\n- **Cleaner codebase:** `src/invoices.js` reduced from 311 lines to 183 lines, `src/totals.js` focused on calculation logic",
